  "question_stem": "A bus travels between two stops, $A$ and $B$. The bus starts from rest at $A$ and accelerates at a constant rate of $a \\text{ m s}^{-2}$ until it reaches a speed of $16 \\text{ m s}^{-1}$. It then travels at this constant speed before decelerating at a constant rate of $0.75a \\text{ m s}^{-2}$, coming to rest at $B$. The total time for the journey is $240 \\text{ s}$.",
  "context_texts": [
    "$T=240-\\left(\\frac{16}{a}+\\frac{64}{3a}\\right)$ for the constant-speed time."
  ],
